## Acceptance and review

Account for every target. Preserve scope, accepted identity, protected content, deliberate exceptions, and the selected generation setting. Coordinate the requested content and placement intent into a complete responsive layout. Implement actual browser behavior; disclose missing configuration. Preview and exported behavior must agree. Describe component choices, proposed identity/decision changes, and concrete design criticism. Never silently apply a new project-wide rule or replace an intentional style solely to follow a convention.
